rmat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FORSCHUNGSZENTRUM KARLSRUHE GMBH</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RUTHER, PATRICK</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>RUTHER PATRICK</name><address><country>DE</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RUTHER, PATRICK</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical position sensor provided with an input optical fiber (2), output optical fibers (3, 4), a flat light conductor (6) disposed on a substrate (1) and having a branched light conductor (14), a first columnar lens (11) adapted to transform the optical path of the light wave projected from the flat light conductor (6) and focus the light wave onto the surface to be detected, and a second columnar lens (12) adapted to transform the optical path of the light wave reflected off the surface to be detected and introduce the light wave into the flat light conductor (6).  This configuration provides a small optical position sensor that has good detection characteristics even over long measurement distances.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un capteur optique de position comportant une fibre optique (2) d'entrée, des fibres (3, 4) optiques de sortie ; un conducteur (6) de lumière plat placé sur un substrat (1) et comportant un conducteur (14) de lumière ramifié ; une première lentille colonnaire (11) conçue pour modifier le parcours optique de l'onde lumineuse provenant du conducteur (6) de lumière plat et concentrer l'onde lumineuse sur la surface à détecter ; et une deuxième lentille colonnaire (12) conçue pour modifier le parcours optique de l'onde lumineuse reflétée hors de la surface à détecter et introduire l'onde lumineuse dans le conducteur (6) de lumière plat. Cette configuration permet d'obtenir un capteur optique de position présentant de bonnes caractéristiques de détection, même sur de longues distances de mesure.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>